{
 "id": "remote_causal",
 "version": "1.0.0",
 "depends_on": [],
 "area": "retina",
 "description": "REMOTE CAUSATION (block 228000): the only-other salient thing is a SWITCH; interacting with it affects a REMOTE thing (the deferred Doom problem: switch here -> door there). EXHAUSTION-FIRST: try the known option (rc_try_known), exhaust + break the futile cycle (rc_exhausted, 226), EXPLORE the un-visited salient object (rc_seek_novel_salient \u2014 visited/salience only, NO causal model), INTERVENE on arrival, POSIT+CONFIRM the remote-causal link by the do-contrast (rc_posit_link -> rc_confirm_interventional: eff_act==1 AND eff_noop==0, attributing across space; rc_refute_interventional; rc_attribute_remote), then ACT (rc_act_seek_confirmed -> rc_pass). Controls: causal_prior (no exploration), local_only (attributes only at B's location), no_intervention (passive co-occurrence -> confabulates). Domain-agnostic (no ls20/doom/cross/lever token); same rules run ls20 cross->shape AND Doom lever->door. Guarded on game.remote_on==1 (default-OFF, byte-identical) + game.arm. Integer-native; no Rust; reuses the 227 posit/confirm + 210 operate + 220 nav + 226 frustration.",
 "microtheory": {
  "name": "remote_causal",
  "description": "A salient object can affect a REMOTE thing across space. The agent explores the un-visited salient object out of exhaustion (no prior causal belief), intervenes, and DISCOVERS the remote-causal link by the interventional do-contrast (act->effect vs no-op->no-effect), attributing B's change to the remote action across space; then acts on the confirmed link. Every decision is a rule."
 },
